2026-07-29 20:46:04,363 INFO {"timestamp": "2026-07-30T00:46:04.363998", "employee_id": "1001", "response": {"allowed": true, "response": {"status": "SUCCESS", "agents": ["policy"], "results": [{"intent": "policy_search", "data": {"ids": [["pto", "fmla", "Bereavement Leave"]], "embeddings": null, "documents": [["Paid Time Off (PTO)\n\nEmployees accrue PTO based on years of service.\n\nVacation requests should normally be submitted\nat least two weeks before the requested leave.\n\nManager approval is required.\n\nUnused PTO may carry forward according\nto company policy.", "Family Medical Leave (FMLA)\n\nEligible employees may take up to 12 weeks of unpaid,\njob-protected leave during a rolling 12-month period.\n\nReasons include:\n\n\u2022 Birth of a child\n\n\u2022 Adoption\n\n\u2022 Serious medical condition\n\n\u2022 Caring for a spouse\n\n\u2022 Caring for a parent\n\n\u2022 Caring for a child\n\nMedical certification may be required.\n\nHR approval is required.", "Bereavement Leave\n\nEmployees receive up to five paid working days\nfollowing the death of an immediate family member.\n\nAdditional unpaid leave may be approved by HR."]], "uris": null, "included": ["metadatas", "documents", "distances"], "data": null, "metadatas": [[{"source": "docs\\pto.md", "title": "pto"}, {"source": "docs\\fmla.md", "title": "fmla"}, {"source": "docs\\Bereavement Leave.md", "title": "Bereavement Leave"}]], "distances": [[0.5952081084251404, 0.6558243036270142, 0.6937328577041626]]}}]}}}
